  - The high-tech sleekness comes about via the dark background, glowing cyan UI elements, angular frames, and sci-fi typography.
  - It can be concisely described as exuding "paradoxical complexity and sophistication".

### Presentation

Elaborating on this concept a bit further, this means intelligently grouping functions for presentation only when dynamically needed. The presentation utilizes styles such as accordions, slide outs, pop overs, etc. Essentially, adopting the motto "Out of sight out of mind". In other words, if we arent using it there is no reason for it to display. Inversely, when the tools/functions/buttons are needed they should dynamically present themeselves in a snappy and "HUD" like way. 

>Here are some examples of how to go from a static monolith to a modern and dynamic HUD-like experience:

- What currently houses the selectable modes of 'Debug', 'Single Review', and 'Compare' can be termed as a dock (thats being generous). To make it dynamic we could use a drop-down when hovered over for example.

- Regarding the toasts actually, this needs to be more cohesively implemented as well. We currently see the toast when clicking the url share button, exporting a session and Im not sure where else and that the point. This needs to be cohesively integrated throughout all aspects of the app. 

# Summary

Overall, the app is missing a certain fluidity and  cohesion between components. Rather than feeling "connected" the components feel individualized and "klunky". The correct aesthetic should cause a user to describe their experience as intuitive and snappy. Then you will know you have achieved the vision.

